# Photos -- what the viewer may DO. The other half is photos.ns, which says
# what it may NAME; the kernel enforces both, and a class here can only ever
# narrow what the session already holds.
#
# A picture viewer runs a DECODER over files it did not write, which is the
# same exposure a browser has in miniature: a malformed JPEG is an attacker's
# input reaching a Huffman decoder. So it gets the two classes it cannot work
# without and nothing else -- no network, no audio, no USB, no raw disk. A bug
# in the resampler cannot reach a device that was never granted.

filesystem     # read the pictures, and the font the chrome is set in
gpu            # a window is a GPU resource -- without this it cannot draw
